message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Iron Dome"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-05-22
authors:
  - name: KirkForge
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/kirkforge/IronDome"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kirkforge/IronDome"
keywords:
  - sandbox
  - seccomp
  - behavioral-analysis
  - supply-chain
  - security
  - deterministic
  - irondome
abstract: >-
  Iron Dome is a deterministic runtime sandbox and behavioral analysis engine
  for supply-chain security. It couples real kernel-level sandboxing (seccomp-bpf
  on Linux, seatbelt on macOS) with multi-signal behavioral detection — timing
  anomalies, data exfiltration, entropy spikes, honeypot access, and baseline
  drift — to catch threats that static scanners miss. Iron Dome is the L3/L4
  runtime companion to PicoSentry (L2 static scanner), completing a layered
  defense-in-depth pipeline from install to execution.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "PicoSentry"
    version: 0.15.0
    url: "https://github.com/kirkforge/PicoSentry"
    description: >-
      L2 deterministic offline npm/pnpm supply-chain scanner — the static
      analysis companion that runs before Iron Dome's runtime sandboxing.